[6.2509, "o", "\r\n"]
[6.3869, "o", "Checking this Mac. This can take a minute.\r\n"]
[7.359, "o", "\r\nWhat I found\r\n  macOS 26.6.2 (arm64)\r\n  Homebrew: Homebrew 7.0.12\r\n  Installed with: install script (git checkout)\r\n  Owner of /opt/homebrew: admin\r\n  Files with a different owner: 0\r\n  People accounts on this Mac: 2 (2 use Homebrew)\r\n\r\nResult\r\n  - A person's account ('admin') owns /opt/homebrew. Other users get 'not writable' errors.\r\n  - 2 people use Homebrew on this Mac, so they will collide.\r\n  - The brew wrapper is missing for: admin bob.\r\n\r\n"]
[7.3594, "o", "Name for the hidden Homebrew account [homebrew]: "]
[8.8672, "o", "h"]
[8.9316, "o", "o"]
[8.9964, "o", "m"]
[9.0617, "o", "e"]
[9.1269, "o", "b"]
[9.192, "o", "r"]
[9.255, "o", "e"]
[9.3187, "o", "w"]
[9.3829, "o", "\r\n"]
[9.408, "o", "Plan\r\n"]
[9.4283, "o", "  1. Create the administrator account 'homebrew' (UID 600) with a random password.\r\n  2. Hide it and set its shell to /usr/bin/false (nobody can log in with it).\r\n  3. Run: chown -R homebrew:admin /opt/homebrew ; chmod -R g-w,o-w /opt/homebrew\r\n  4. Put the brew wrapper in /usr/local/share/homebrew-shared-mac and add it to ~/.zshrc of: admin bob\r\n  5. Check the result.\r\nEvery change is saved in /usr/local/share/homebrew-shared-mac/backups.\r\nUndo everything: sudo ./scripts/setup.sh --rollback\r\n\r\n"]
[9.4283, "o", "Make these changes now? [y/N] "]
[16.4542, "o", "y"]
[16.5189, "o", "\r\n"]
[16.581, "o", "Creating the hidden account 'homebrew'...\r\n"]
[18.5648, "o", "Created the hidden account 'homebrew'.\r\n"]
[19.6153, "o", "Changed the owner of /opt/homebrew to 'homebrew'.\r\n"]
[19.6322, "o", "Added the wrapper to /Users/admin/.zshrc\r\n"]
[19.6488, "o", "Added the wrapper to /Users/bob/.zshrc\r\n"]
[20.9281, "o", "PASS  'homebrew' owns every file in /opt/homebrew\r\n"]
[20.9566, "o", "PASS  brew --version works for admin\r\nPASS  wrapper is in /usr/local/share/homebrew-shared-mac\r\n"]
[21.0242, "o", "PASS  a new Terminal window loads the wrapper\r\nPASS  no --appdir setting and no brew app in a ~/Applications folder\r\n\r\nNext\r\n  1. Close this Terminal window and open a new one.\r\n     Only a new window loads the wrapper. (Or run: source ~/.zshrc)\r\n  2. Test it (this asks for YOUR password): brew update\r\n     If brew says 'not writable' and shows 'sudo chown', do not run that command.\r\n     It means this window does not have the wrapper yet. Open a new window.\r\n  3. Tell the other people to open a new Terminal window too.\r\n     The script already added the wrapper to their ~/.zshrc.\r\n"]
[21.026, "o", "\r\nUndo all of it: sudo ./scripts/setup.sh --rollback\r\nReport for your AI agent: /Users/admin/shared-brew-report-20261125-040110.txt\r\n"]
[21.026, "o", "The report lists the account names on this Mac. Read it before you share it.\r\n"]
